statement:
Determine all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ for which:
\begin{itemize}
\item $n$ is not the square of any integer,
\item $\lfloor \sqrt{n} \rfloor^3$ divides $n^2$.
\end{itemize}

For positive integers $n$, define $A(n) = \dfrac{(2n)!}{(n!)^2}$. Determine the sets of positive integers $n$ for which
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] $A(n)$ is an even number,
\item[(b)] $A(n)$ is a multiple of $4$.
\end{enumerate}
